                <head>124. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On June 5, Elim O’Shaughnessy called on Chancellor Adenauer to discuss European security, but before he was able to
                    present the United States view, the Chancellor “launched into a long tirade”
                    against a paper which had been submitted by Harold
                        Stassen to the United Nations Disarmament Subcommittee. For
                    O’Shaughnessy’s report on this meeting and related documentation, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1955-57v20/pg_604">volume XX, pages 604</ref> ff.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
